your rounds otherwise. In either case, output the fully self contained rigorous and cohesive report detailing your argument\\n\"}]},{\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"id\":\"item-1943\",\"summary\":[\"**Clarifying scope for study folder inspection**\"],\"content\":[]},{\"type\":\"agentMessage\",\"id\":\"item-1944\",\"text\":\"I’ll use the rigorous-math workflow and keep the project-file boundary exactly at `studies/mean_field_peeling` (plus new temporary artifacts I create). I’ll first recover the two claimed results, then reconstruct one self-contained theorem/report and subject each revision to blind proof, scope, and source-theorem audits.\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"},{\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"id\":\"item-1945\",\"summary\":[\"**Planning audit of finite-moment no-go theorem**\"],\"content\":[]},{\"type\":\"agentMessage\",\"id\":\"item-1946\",\"text\":\"The two claims are in the same study lineage, but the earlier “closure-search” documents were superseded. The current candidate is the fully trainable depth-three report under `identity_compiler/linear_gaussian_program/depth3_unfrozen_readout_closure`: it contains both the trace-class/free-Wishart IDE and a finite-scalar moment no-go. I’m treating those as claims to re-prove, not as established facts.\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"},{\"type\":\"subAgentActivity\",\"id\":\"call_0h7P4qLFKRQC3agVWXFM8qJB\",\"kind\":\"interacted\",\"agentThreadId\":\"01a0490b-21d8-7100-8b61-aefc1b5b20dd\",\"agentPath\":\"/root/l2_blind_continuum_r4\"},{\"type\":\"subAgentActivity\",\"id\":\"call_vhdHHSPIGJ4sidazmAI12QHf\",\"kind\":\"interacted\",\"agentThreadId\":\"01a0490b-0cee-7511-b6e7-6b3f55613f9c\",\"agentPath\":\"/root/l2_blind_source_r4\"},{\"type\":\"subAgentActivity\",\"id\":\"call_Qk02WOVM8a7n7eD8840tSdzh\",\"kind\":\"interacted\",\"agentThreadId\":\"01a0490b-0cee-7511-b6e7-6b3f55613f9c\",\"agentPath\":\"/root/l2_blind_source_r4\"},{\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"id\":\"item-1947\",\"summary\":[\"**Auditing operator norm and rank estimates**\",\