han silently inheriting them.  In the transpose-adjunction Case 2\\n\",\"truncated\":false}}]},{\"type\":\"fileChange\",\"id\":\"exec-1a0ab926-7621-4b7f-979e-cf7a3f146baf\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"changes\":[{\"path\":\"/tmp/L2_FULL_AUDITED_PROOF.md\",\"kind\":{\"type\":\"update\",\"move_path\":null},\"diff\":{\"text\":\"@@ -1038,2 +1038,34 @@\\n \\n+Three earlier/later displays require the following additional corrections.\\n+In the simultaneous Gaussian-conditioning lemma (source lines 243--278),\\n+the conditional mean is\\n+\\\\[\\n+E=ZQ^+ +P^{+\\\\top}X^\\\\top-P^{+\\\\top}P^\\\\top ZQ^+;     \\\\tag{A.1}\\n+\\\\]\\n+the source's \\\\(Y\\\\) is undefined and must be \\\\(Z\\\\), and the Lagrange\\n+multiplier calculation requires \\\\(Q^+\\\\), not \\\\(Q^\\\\top\\\\).  Direct\\n+multiplication, using the compatibility \\\\(X^\\\\top Q=P^\\\\top Z\\\\), verifies\\n+\\\\(EQ=Z\\\\) and \\\\(P^\\\\top E=X^\\\\top\\\\); the displayed Lagrange stationarity\\n+then proves that (A.1) is the minimum-Frobenius-norm solution.  The\\n+orthogonal Gaussian remainder in the lemma is therefore unchanged.\\n+\\n+In the projected-variance rewrite (source lines 1866--1869), with\\n+\\\\(\\\\gamma=Y^\\\\top h/n\\\\) and \\\\(\\\\Upsilon=Y^\\\\top Y/n\\\\), the exact identity is\\n+\\\\[\\n+\\\\sigma^2=\\\\sigma_A^2\\\\left(\\\\frac{h^\\\\top h}{n}\\n+                         -\\\\gamma^\\\\top\\\\Upsilon^+\\\\gamma\\\\right), \\\\tag{A.2}\\n+\\\\]\\n+because \\\\(Y^\\\\top h=n\\\\gamma\\\\) and\\n+\\\\((Y^\\\\top Y)^+=n^{-1}\\\\Upsilon^+\\\\).  This is precisely the expression whose\\n+limit the next source line states.  Finally, at source lines 3663--3668,\\n+\\\\[\\n+\\\\frac1n\\\\sum_\\\\alpha\\n+\\\\max(\\\\sigma^2d_\\\\alpha,\\\\mathring\\\\sigma^2)^p\\n+\\\\le\\\\max(\\\\sigma^2,\\\\mathring\\\\sigma^2)^p,             \\\\tag{A.3}\\n+\\\\]\\n+not the same maximum to the power \\\\(p/2\\\\).  Since\\n+\\\\(\\\\sigma\\\\to\\\\mathring\\\\sigma\\\\), (A.3) has the uniform boundedness required\\n+there.  None of (A.1)--(A.3) alters a definition or a subsequent estimate;\\n+they repair the literal algebra used to reach the intended quantities.\\n+\\n Two printed auxiliary claims were deliberately excluded after source-level\\n\",\"truncated\":false}}]},{\"type\":\"subAgentActivity\",\"id\":\"call_Xcrtluy4n20jjJ036Rhc2ya9\",\"kind\":\"started\",\"agentThreadId\":\"01a0490b-0cee-7511-b6e7-6b3f55613f9c\",\"agentPath\":\"/root/l2_blind_source_r4\"},{\"type\":\"subAgentActivity\",\"id\":\"call_g9sMlvkUWAgEWtseGRVabn28\",\"kind\":\"started\",\"agentThreadId\":\"01a0490b-21d8-7100-8b61-aefc1b5b20dd\",\"agentPath\":\"/root/l2_blind_continuum_r4\"},{\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"id\":\"item-1934\",\"summary\":[\"**Reviewing action patch consistency**\",\"**Clarifying theorem assumptions and proof validity**\",\"**Reviewing action patch consistency**\",\"**Clarifying theorem assumptions and proof validity**\"],\"content\":[]},{\"type\":\"agentMessage\",\"id\":\"item-1935\",\"text\":\"The source ledger now contains all six defects found across two independent readings, together with the corrected identities and why each correction preserves the theorem’s proof:\\n\\n- two transpose-conditioning symbols,\\n- one collision exponent,\\n- one conditional variance,\\n- the simultaneous Gaussian-conditioning mean,\\n- one missing normalization factor,\\n- and one false exponent in a boundedness line.\\n\\nA fourth fresh source referee is rereading the complete corrected proof chain, while another fresh referee is checking the internal mean-field/gradient-flow argument.\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"},{\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"id\":\"item-1936\",\"summary\":[\"**Assessing operator norm bounds**\",\"**Verifying formal operator linearity and consistency**\",\"**Assessing operator norm bounds**\",\"**Verifying formal operator linearity and consistency**\",\"**Assessing operator norm bounds**\",\"**Verifying formal operator linearity and consistency**\",\"**Confirming W2 convergence and cross-time record needs**\"],\"content\":[]},{\"type\":\"subAgentActivity\",\"id\":\"subagent-completed-01a0490b-2214-76b1-a373-ecedcde6efb8\",\"kind\":\"completed\",\"agentThreadId\":\"01a0490b-21d8-7100-8b61-aefc1b5b20dd\",\"agentPath\":\"/root/l2_blind_continuum_r4\"},{\"type\":\"subAgentActivity\",\"id\":\"subagent-completed-01a0490b-0d33-7033-9785-a01c1a82ce41\",\"kind\":\"completed\",\"agentThreadId\":\"01a0490b-0cee-7511-b6e7-6b3f55613f9c\",\"agentPath\":\"/root/l2_blind_source_r4\"},{\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"id\":\"item-1937\",\"summary\":[\"**Planning final isolated audit run**\"],\"content\":[]},{\"type\":\"agentMessage\",\"id\":\"item-1938\",\"text\":\"The final frozen manuscript has now passed both last-round isolated audits cleanly:\\n\\n- the source referee reread the full primary proof with all six corrections and found no remaining consequence-level defect;\\n- the continuum referee independently passed the typed action state, nested reused-operator induction, mesh order, exact-GD observables, path laws, and restartability.\\n\\nEarlier rounds did fail and force substantive repairs; I have preserved those failures and corrections in the report rather than presenting the first draft as valid.\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"},{\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"id\":\"item-1939\",\"summary\":[\"**Planning final summary and report**\",\"**Summarizing corrected theorem validity**\",\"**Planning final summary and report**\",\"**Summarizing corrected theorem validity**\",\"**Confirming final report content and citations**\"],\"content\":[]},{\"type\":\"agentMessage\",\"id\":\"item-1940\",\"text\":\"Yes. The construction is valid, but the earlier proof was not valid as originally written. After repairing its internal gaps and six errors in the cited paper’s printed proof, the result is unconditional.\\n\\nThe verified scaling is\\n\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\phi=\\\\arctan,\\\\qquad\\n(\\\\sigma_{1,n}^2,\\\\sigma_{2,n}^2,\\\\sigma_{3,n}^2)\\n=(1,n^{-1},n^{-4}),\\n\\\\]\\n\\n\\\\[\\n(\\\\lambda_n^{(1)},\\\\lambda_n^{(2)},\\\\lambda_n^{(3)})\\n=(n,1,n^{-1}),\\\\qquad\\n\\\\eta_n=n^{-2}.\\n\\\\]\\n\\nThus\\n\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\eta_n\\\\lambda_n^{(1)}=n^{-1},\\\\quad\\n\\\\eta_n\\\\lambda_n^{(2)}=n^{-2},\\\\quad\\n\\\\eta_n\\\\lambda_n^{(3)}=n^{-3}.\\n\\\\]\\n\\nAlong the full width sequence, exact GD converges jointly on compact time intervals to a unique autonomous action-law gradient flow. Both hidden layers learn features, all parameter blocks remain active, the nonlinear residuals stay positive, the kernel changes, and the loss decreases on a common nonzero interval.\\n\\nThe proof now includes:\\n\\n- a fixed canonical \\\\(L^2\\\\)-operator realization;\\n- explicit reused-\\\\(B/B^\\\\top\\\\) response terms;\\n- an exact population-oracle residual recursion;\\n- a typed action-state metric and induction over arbitrary nested operator probes;\\n- width-first, fixed-mesh identification without a growing tensor program;\\n- quantitative uniform-integrability and truncation arguments;\\n- exact-GD state, kernel, velocity, and \\\\(W_2\\\\)-path convergence;\\n- direct positive small-time coefficients for both hidden layers.\\n\\nThe external input is the fixed-program Master Theorem from [Yang, Tensor Programs III, v3](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2009.10685v3). Its complete proof was audited. Six printed algebra/notation errors were identified and explicitly repaired in the report; the corrected proof still establishes the theorem used here. No DMFT result, growing-step tensor theorem, or questionable appendix strengthening is invoked.\\n\\nThe complete frozen report is here:\\n\\n[Full self-contained audited L=2 proof](/tmp/L2_FULL_AUDITED_PROOF.md)\\n\\nSHA-256:\\n\\n```text\\ne9f963cde5061f4f5b4d8d3913a62ccd013af451334e46356134f624759d42fb\\n```\\n\\nThe final round passed two fresh isolated audits cleanly: one source-level audit of the external theorem and one adversarial audit of the full continuum and exact-GD argument.\",\"phas