\\) calls grows like \\\\(T/h\\\\). [Primary theorem](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2009.10685v3)\\n- The proposed all-source lemma was internally inconsistent and did not control the full forward/adjoint response history, particularly near singular Gaussian Grams.\\n- The trigonometric identity for \\\\(\\\\phi=\\\\sin+\\\\cos\\\\) does not repair this: the gate \\\\(\\\\phi'(S)P_2\\\\) has an unbounded partial linearization on \\\\(L^2\\\\).\\n- Consequently, cutoff removal, compact-time convergence, \\\\(W_2\\\\) path convergence, uniqueness, and restartability remain unproved.\\n\\nWhat remains valid is:\\n\\n- the exact finite-width normalization and gradient equations;\\n- width convergence for every fixed finite number of steps via a population-oracle tensor program;\\n- the two initialization response operators;\\n- the positive-definiteness calculations;\\n- the conditional small-time feature, kernel, and loss coefficients.\\n\\nA second fresh blind-audit round returned CLEAN on this corrected classification—open rather than proved or disproved. The complete self-contained report is here:\\n\\n[Audited L=3 report](/tmp/L3_AUDITED_REPORT.md)\\n\\nThe missing ingredient is a new representation-invariant, program-length-uniform aggregate-adjoint theorem controlling dense reused-matrix histories at singular covariance. Without that theorem, presenting a complete \\\\(L=3\\\\) proof would be fabricating the central bridge. No project files were inspected.\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}]},{\"id\":\"01a044ce-acc2-7773-97fa-78e954c53bb3\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"error\":null,\"startedAt\":1787860790,\"completedAt\":1787862199,\"durationMs\":1409460,\"items\":[{\"type\":\"userMessage\",\"id\":\"item-1441\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"ok, can you go one level deeper into this invoked theorem, and its proof, digest it fully, and see if after rigorously evaluating it, the statement has to fundumentally change in a way that would create a gap in our proof, or the cited theorem as it currently stand and we need is correct as stated and thus our result also stands correct unconditionally. resolve this completely&#x20;\\n\"}]},{\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"id\":\"item-1442\",\"summary\":[\"**Planning rigorous Han theorem audit**\"],\"content\":[]},{\"type\":\"agentMessage\",\"id\":\"item-1443\",\"text\":\"I’m using the rigorous-math workflow because this is now a theorem-provenance question, not merely an invocation check. I’ll trace Han’s proof down to the underlying AMP leave-one-out results, verify every extension actually needed by our finite-stage OMFP program, and run independent proof-chain and counterexample audits. I will not inspect any project files.\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"},{\"type\":\"agentMessage\",\"id\":\"item-1444\",\"text\":\"The first proof-chain issue is already sharply identified: Han’s fixed-stage GFOM theorem is broader than Bao–Han–Xu’s memory-one AMP theorem. The decisive question is whether Han’s passage to history-dependent asymmetric AMP is a proved finite-dimensional augmentation/reduction or only an assertion. I’m auditing that exact bridge, including singular covariances and coordinate-dependent maps.\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"},{\"type\":\"subAgentActivity\",\"id\":\"call_SaaJqYczqPFjk2dRmo6Vmo77\",\"kind\":\"started\",\"agentThreadId\":\"01a044ce-e236-7130-88bc-c8bc50ebe777\",\"agentPath\":\"/root/han_full_proof_audit\"},{\"type\":\"subAgentActivity\",\"id\":\"call_98YZwjwaEPS4XQX5xiQs8HKp\",\"kind\":\"started\",\"agentThreadId\":\"01a044ce-f318-71b3-ac8d-209a5aac6ffb\",\"agentPath\":\"/root/bao_extension_audit\"},{\"type\":\"subAgentActivity\",\"id\":\"call_kmSk23Mhb8lfF1LYj0CYKT2W\",\"kind\":\"started\",\"agentThreadId\":\"01a044cf-05b0-7ee0-b8bc-31c1800086ba\",\"agentPath\":\"/root/alternative_theorem_route\"},{\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"id\":\"item-1445\",\"summary\":[\"**Investigating full-history AMP state augmentation**\",\"**Analyzing vector AMP long-memory limitations and proofs**\",\"*